<h1>Fan-out to multiple destinations</h1>
<p>A common architecture pattern is to stream events from a single source system to multiple destinations. This recipe shows how to set up parallel pipelines so events reach warehouses, real-time analytics platforms, and operational databases simultaneously.</p>

<h2>Overview</h2>
<p>Fan-out workflows let you:</p>
<ul>
<li>Maintain a single source of truth while serving multiple downstream systems</li>
<li>Process the same events through different <a href="/guides/transforming-events-in-flight">transforms</a> for each destination</li>
<li>Decouple destination failures from affecting other pipelines</li>
</ul>

<h2>Creating multiple pipelines</h2>
<p>Create a separate <a href="/concepts-pipelines">pipeline</a> for each destination, all reading from the same source <a href="/concepts-connectors">connector</a>:</p>

<div class='code-block'>
